{"path":"thread/lock_guard/lock_guard","title":"std::lock_guard<Mutex>::lock_guard","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::lock_guard&lt;Mutex&gt;::</span>lock_guard","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/lock_guard/lock_guard","section":"thread","kind":"page","summary":"Acquires ownership of the given mutex m.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">explicit</span> lock_guard<span class=\"br0\">(</span> mutex_type<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> m <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">lock_guard<span class=\"br0\">(</span> mutex_type<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> m, <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/lock_tag\"><span class=\"kw2183\">std::<span class=\"me2\">adopt_lock_t</span></span></a> t <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">lock_guard<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> lock_guard<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> delete<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Acquires ownership of the given mutex <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m</span></code>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Effectively calls <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m.<span class=\"me1\">lock</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Acquires ownership of the mutex <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m</span></code> without attempting to lock it. The behavior is undefined if the current thread does not hold a non-shared lock (i.e., a lock acquired by <code>lock</code>, <code>try_lock</code>, <code>try_lock_for</code>, or <code>try_lock_until</code>) on <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m</span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">3)</span> Copy constructor is deleted.</div>\n<p>The behavior is undefined if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m</span></code> is destroyed before the <code>lock_guard</code> object is.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> m\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> mutex to acquire ownership of\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> t\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> tag parameter used to select non-locking version of the constructor\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Throws any exceptions thrown by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">m.<span class=\"me1\">lock</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Throws nothing.</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"thread","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"},{"path":"thread/lock_guard","title":"std::lock_guard"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::lock_guard<Mutex>::lock_guard","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"3 declarations; revisions: since C++11. Acquires ownership of the given mutex m."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"m, t"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"Throws any exceptions thrown by m.lock()."}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":124,"codeBlockCount":0}
